# Development workflow

- Treat the local repository as the source workspace. Write and review code locally.
- Run relevant local checks before publishing changes.
- Keep `main` deployable. Commit verified changes and push them to GitHub.
- Production deploys automatically from `main` through the repository GitHub Actions workflow.
- Never edit application source directly on the server.
- After every deployment, verify both the GitHub Actions result and the live application.
- Run the application on the server through Docker Compose and Caddy.
- Keep secrets and private SSH keys out of Git and application files.
- Do not weaken SSH restrictions or expose administrative ports for deployment.
